Sol-Intentwright: Lares (Tasked Spirit) / Ink-Clerk:

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/1-observe-standing-ground`>>

!! 1. ✶ Observe — standing ground

''MEASURED.'' `I1` follows the sealed anchor; Wave C, K15-H and Wave D landed ([[road:487,459|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem]]). No production <code>&#64;intents-</code> plane surfaced in the code search. The carrier already names five planes, while the current derivation and ring enumerate four ([[persona-scope.ts:121|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-scope.ts]], [[persona-group-ring.ts:136|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-group-ring.ts]]). The shared HMAC tag derives from the PersonaGroup ID; one bag name follows each relation ([[persona-scope.ts:81|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-scope.ts]]). Founding creates plane documents and bootstrap entries; a `plane` act in signed <code>&#64;persona</code> must vouch for each URL before registration. The verifier re-derives canonical bytes, checks Ed25519 and authorizes against face anchor/KEL; the projector admits only URLs backed by those acts ([[init.ts:129|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/commands/init.ts]], [[signed-act.ts:2|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/signed-act.ts]], [[persona-act.ts:96|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-act.ts]]). Node registers all proven held planes and mounts the worn face; browser registers after face proof ([[open-node-vessel.ts:2200|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts]], [[open-browser-vessel.ts:1181|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts]]). The ring lets each face's own devices sync governed documents ([[persona-group-ring.ts:136|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-group-ring.ts]]); the herm carries without opening them. Wave D seals atom and anchor as separate face custody rows under each face's FCK; the plane itself retains its distinct rest/wire seal rules ([[k15-wave-d-lane.mem:33|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane.mem]], [[plane-seal.ts:5|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/plane-seal.ts]]).

''MEASURED.'' Node loads the worn face's atom from custody; browser derives its atom key from that face's seed. The device seed serves substrate duties; the atom signs face proof and face acts ([[open-node-vessel.ts:1887|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts]], [[open-browser-vessel.ts:686|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts]], [[open-browser-vessel.ts:861|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts]]). Today a remote summons lands in the daemon Automerge doc, each daemon dispatcher converts it to local volatile invocation, tombstones transport, and writes an outcome back to the daemon doc; each vessel runs its own daemon VM ([[verb-dispatcher.ts:1|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/verb-dispatcher.ts]]). `face-join` runs there, rejects joinee self-seating, then records its grant on <code>&#64;persona</code>; two hearths can still re-key before either sees an outcome ([[operator-daemon-behavior.ts:601|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts]], [[face-join.ts:189|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-keyhive/src/face-join.ts]]). Reactors register in the daemon island, sometimes posting pool work to main; browser composes the same island/dispatcher. The CLI names a face per invocation ([[operator-daemon-behavior.ts:371|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts]], [[daemon-behavior.ts:182|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/daemon-behavior.ts]], [[CHANGELOG.md:17|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/CHANGELOG.md]]).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/3-orient-red-first-lane-slices`>>

!! 3. ⏿ Orient — red-first lane slices

''LEAD.'' One I1 lane should carry a single wire image and node/browser parity through the summons cutover; place relay research and build in a later lane. Each red below needs its named passing control.

# ''Plane and image:'' red: two faces cross-read, a late joinee misses the plane, unsigned URL registers, or plane projects; controls: same-face sync, signed URL registration, projected wiki file. Hold `persona-scope`, `register-bags`, `persona-group-ring`, founding/admit bundles, signed act/projector, node/browser openers, seal and mirror guards.
# ''Execution:'' red: prior outcome still triggers effect; wrong pinned atom acts; class-addressed single-effect issues. Controls: fresh intent acts; matching pinned atom acts. Hold shared `intent-plane`/verb policy and both daemon composers/dispatcher bridges.
# ''Fold:'' red: partitioned idempotent duplicate, replay with same nonce, `every` reduced to one slot, claim zombie after takeover, injected clock read. Controls: fresh nonce changes ID; fenced current claimant acts; one outcome per `every` device. Hold shared image/verifier/fold plus effect adapters.
# ''Void and join:'' red: sleeping device acts after observed cancel/revocation/roster edge; two hearths re-key one joinee. Controls: unbounded intent acts; one hearth grants and second stands down; CLI-selected face reaches its own plane. Hold face-join, operation store, daemon behavior and node/browser join bridges.
# ''Read pane and rubric:'' red: pane writes through, keystrokes/save emit intent, duplicate-answer counter silently reads zero. Controls: committed move emits one intent/outcome; seeded duplicate trips counter; projected wiki still mirrors while intent plane does not. Hold daemon wiki view, UI bridge and instrumentation.

''MEASURED overlap.'' W14–W16 touch `place-floor-pin`, `admit-gate-pin`, card filing and `nexus-contract`; K17 touches frontier/lease/realm boards; W26 slice 5 touches a sealed floor accept row per (face, Nexus) ([[road:512|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem]], [[road:515|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem]]). I1 should consume their verified frontier/face readers and avoid editing those files; a shared composer hunk needs one owner at integration. Their signed acts never substitute for intent outcomes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/2-decide-model-joints`>>

!! 2. ◇ Decide — model joints

''Canon rules:'' the carrier explicitly orders `intent/outcome/asks/answer/claim/release/takeover/supersede/cancel`, four audience modes, hash of issuer/verb/arguments/nonce, empty nonce for idempotent verbs, outcome cause/signer, preference winner then lowest `H(atom ‖ intent id)`, no timed expiry, operator release priority, causal voids, late `every` membership, and single-effect refusal for class/any-device ([[carrier:47–92|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem]]). A duplicate winner changes the read, never undoes an effect. House law ''no global now'' forbids timestamp arbitration; ''one name, one relation'' calls for one shared image; ''isomorphic by intent'' calls for one fold on both hosts. The rubric rules cross-device, settled, answerable authority decisions and excludes bodies, keystrokes and ordinary wiki saves; the pane reads only ([[carrier:111–139|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem]]).

''Operator-owned choices, with leans:'' (a) Does `answer` assigning an executor replace an invalid unpinned single-effect intent, or only complete an `asks` gate? Lean: require an explicit ask and bind the answer to its ID before execution. (b) Which signed canonical envelope and content hash version binds all kinds, and how do concurrent cancel/takeover/release fold? Lean: domain-separated canonical signed entries with stable IDs, per-intent causal references, authority-first release; never arrival order. (c) What fences an irreversible face-join re-key before outcome visibility? Lean: pinned hearth or preference order plus operation ID checked at the Keyhive effect door; outcome stand-down alone cannot prevent partitioned double action. (d) Does `every` mean joined devices at issue or all later joins until causal bound? Canon selects later joins; decide a bounded roster edge for finite campaigns. (e) How does the view expose duplicate, void-after-act and unknown frontier? Lean: show all, label counted outcome, never hide conflict. These decisions need operator ruling before slice 1 freezes the image.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/4-act-prior-art-and-stories`>>

!! 4. ▶ Act — prior art and stories

''MEASURED outside.'' [[Automerge sync|https://automerge.org/docs/tutorial/local-sync/]] and [[local-first doctrine|https://www.inkandswitch.com/essay/local-first/]] support offline replica convergence; [[Keyhive/Beelay|https://github.com/inkandswitch/keyhive/blob/main/README.md]] supplies signed delegation and authorized sync. [[OTP supervisors|https://www.erlang.org/doc/system/sup_princ.html]] restart local workers, while [[actor mailboxes|https://www.erlang.org/doc/system/ref_man_processes.html]] serialize one actor's intake; neither guarantees one fleet-wide effect. [[Patchwork tasks|https://www.inkandswitch.com/patchwork/notebook/tasks-01/]] show CRDT-carried work; the intent/outcome fold still needs application semantics. [[Kubernetes leader election|https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/cluster-administration/coordinated-leader-election/]] uses renew time, duration and a central compare-and-swap. ''LEAD:'' this house substitutes signed causal bounds, audience slots, idempotent effects and explicit takeover, never a clock lease.

''Gaia.'' Laptop commits “rebuild the wiki” as one intent while phone sleeps. Laptop acts and signs outcome; phone wakes, syncs, sees its slot answered and stands down. If both acted under partition, their idempotency key converges and both receipts remain visible.

''Elyncia.'' Two shrine hearths see one keeper-face join summons. A pinned hearth seats the joinee; the second reads the outcome and stands down. If the first vanishes, a human release/answer redirects through a signed causal act; no sunset clock grants the second permission.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/hooko-aftermath`>>

!! ↺ Hoʻoko / aftermath

''LEAD:'' Rule the five choices above, then cut the red-first lane. Repo inspection only; no suites ran. Next observation should verify the signed image against the live floor/frontier integration head.

